# Commits

Commit **only** when the user asks. Never update git config; never `--force` to main/master; never `--no-verify` / skip hooks unless asked; never `-i` interactive git.

**Amend** only if: user asked (or hook auto-fixed staged files), HEAD is yours this chat, and not pushed. Failed/rejected hook → new commit, never amend.

1. Parallel: `git status`, `git diff` (staged+unstaged), `git log -8 --oneline`.
2. Stage this batch only — never `.env` / secrets (warn if asked).
3. HEREDOC message: English only; `feat:`/`fix:`/`chore:`/`docs:`; 1–2 sentences **why**; no `plan.md` / tor / `Tryb A/B` / `Faza` / `DoD` / `option C`.
4. `git status` after.

Empty tree → no empty commit. Push only if asked.
